{"id":"n-20261028-i0fxh","category":"sports","display_title":"Fleetwood Shocks Arsenal in Cup","display_title_he":"פליטווד מפתיעה את ארסנל בגביע","short_summary":"League Two side Fleetwood Town achieved one of the biggest upsets in English football history by knocking Premier League champions Arsenal out of the Carabao Cup on penalties.","english_level":"C1","words":474,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"BBC Sport","domain":"bbc.co.uk","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cq62y7yzjdmzo","title":"Where does Fleetwood beating Arsenal rank in biggest cup upsets?","published_at":"2026-10-27T23:35:11.000Z"},{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/oct/27/fleetwood-town-arsenal-carabao-cup-fourth-round-match-report","title":"Fantastic Fleetwood seal shootout success in Carabao Cup shock against Arsenal","published_at":"2026-10-27T22:26:05.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-27T22:26:05.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-28T07:00:20.625Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["In what commentators describe as one of the most astonishing upsets in the history of English football, League Two side Fleetwood Town eliminated Premier League champions Arsenal from the Carabao Cup. The dramatic encounter at Highbury Stadium ended in a penalty shootout following a 1-1 draw, sending the fourth-tier club into the quarter-finals of the competition for the very first time.","The evening began with an unordinary atmosphere on the Fylde Coast, featuring a plethora of pyrotechnics that created a red haze across the pitch. Before the action truly settled, the match experienced a six-minute delay when a drone was flown above the stadium, forcing referee Michael Salisbury to lead the players to the sidelines while police searched for the culprit outside the ground. Once play resumed, the hosts stunned the visitors in the 21st minute. Aaron Loupalo-Bi, a young forward on loan from Fulham, brilliantly outsmarted 17-year-old defender Marli Salmon by using his body to shield the ball, spinning away, and slotting a precise shot past Illan Meslier. It was a harsh lesson in senior football for Arsenal's youngsters, exposing the naivety of Mikel Arteta's experimental lineup.","Despite being the dominant force for large portions of the game, Arteta's side struggled to break down a disciplined, robust defense organized by Fleetwood manager Matt Lawlor and his staff. Conditions near the sea, including swirling winds, aided the hosts by holding the ball up in the air and unsettling defenders unaccustomed to coastal gales. Arsenal labored through a pedestrian first half, with Kai Havertz missing their best chance before the break with a wayward header. After the interval, the introduction of Martin Ødegaard injected much-needed cohesion and intensity, effectively acting as a quarterback. Arsenal finally found an equalizer when Viktor Gyokeres bundled home, and though they pushed for a winner—with late chances falling to Ben White and Gyokeres—Fleetwood held firm through resolute defending and crucial late saves from goalkeeper Jay Lynch.","Frustrations boiled over for the Premier League giants late in the match when teenager Max Dowman reacted petulantly to a challenge by Fleetwood enforcer Harrison Neal, earning a straight red card in the 86th minute. Arteta later acknowledged he had already discussed such disciplinary pitfalls with the young player before kickoff.","With the score level after regular time, the match proceeded to a high-stakes penalty shootout. Fleetwood goalkeeper Jay Lynch, a former warehouse worker who spent much of his early career in non-league football, produced a brilliant save against Brazilian international Bruno Guimaraes. Shortly afterward, Conor Haughey smashed his spot-kick into the top corner to seal a 5-3 shootout victory, sparking jubilant scenes of ecstasy on the pitch and in the stands for the Cod Army. For a club that sat 19th in the fourth tier and aimed to earn just 400,000 pounds from the fixture, the night ultimately delivered something truly priceless."],"facts":[{"fact":"Fleetwood Town defeated Arsenal on penalties in the Carabao Cup to reach the quarter-finals for the first time.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Aaron Loupalo-Bi scored the opening goal for Fleetwood in the 21st minute.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Viktor Gyokeres equalized for Arsenal after the break.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Max Dowman was sent off for Arsenal in the 86th minute after a challenge by Harrison Neal.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Fleetwood goalkeeper Jay Lynch saved a penalty from Bruno Guimaraes before Conor Haughey scored the winning penalty in the shootout.","sources":[1,2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"commentators","lemma":"commentator","pos":"noun","he":"מפרשים","name":false},{"text":"describe","lemma":"describe","pos":"verb","he":"מתארים","name":false},{"text":"astonishing","lemma":"astonishing","pos":"adjective","he":"מדהים","name":false},{"text":"upsets","lemma":"upset","pos":"noun","he":"הפתעות / הדחות","name":false},{"text":"history","lemma":"history","pos":"noun","he":"היסטוריה","name":false},{"text":"English","lemma":"English","pos":"adjective","he":"אנגלי","name":true},{"text":"football","lemma":"football","pos":"noun","he":"כדורגל","name":false},{"text":"League Two","lemma":"league two","pos":"noun","he":"ליגה שניה (רביעית)","name":true},{"text":"side","lemma":"side","pos":"noun","he":"קבוצה","name":false},{"text":"Fleetwood Town","lemma":"fleetwood town","pos":"noun","he":"פליטוד טאון","name":true},{"text":"eliminated","lemma":"eliminate","pos":"verb","he":"הדיחה","name":false},{"text":"Premier League","lemma":"premier league","pos":"noun","he":"הפרמיר ליג","name":true},{"text":"champions","lemma":"champion","pos":"noun","he":"אלופים","name":false},{"text":"Arsenal","lemma":"arsenal","pos":"noun","he":"ארסנל","name":true},{"text":"Carab